# Allowlist: only the website, its build kit and the design hand-off go to GitHub.
# The raw source files (NYBG staff list, Forest Plan PDF, draft policy, student decks, readings)
# stay on this computer; the build kit needs them only to regenerate the data.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.github/
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/nybg-guide/
!/guide-build-kit/
!/claude-code-handoff/

# never commit these, even inside the allowed folders
*.zip
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Photos extracted from the decks and the Reference Guide stay local: their licenses are unknown, so the
# site never uses them (build_species.py keeps only openly licensed photos; those are in photos/public/).
/guide-build-kit/photos/*
!/guide-build-kit/photos/public/
